usage
=====

the service loads /etc/nftables.conf at start and flushes the ruleset
when stopped. it does nothing if the file doesn't exist. minimal
example that drops incoming traffic except ssh:

  #!/usr/sbin/nft -f
  flush ruleset

  table inet filter {
      chain input {
          type filter hook input priority 0; policy drop;
          ct state established,related accept
          iif lo accept
          tcp dport 22 accept
          meta l4proto { icmp, ipv6-icmp } accept
      }
  }

enable the service:

  ln -s /etc/sv/nftables /var/service

reload rules after editing:

  sv restart nftables
